A||N||2||turbo86se||Loose rotor?||||5||
Z||000000||turbo86se||05-26-2000||07:03 PM||||<BR>Hey guys, I'm trying to find the light thumping sound coming from my rear wheel area. So far I've pulled off the rear wheel, and I've discovered the rotor has some play to it. just a little, but maybe it is causing the noise.<BR>I found out the high pitches noise is from my steel-braided brake line not fastened to the wheel well, and it was rubbing the tire.<BR>Is the rotor supposed to have any play to it? Thanks!!!!||||reg||5
Z||000001||batboy||05-26-2000||07:31 PM||||On the rear rotors, if you have the wheel off, nothing is holding it on except the caliper. So yes, it will be a little loose. Once the lug nuts are torqued back down, the rotor is firmly secured.||||reg||1
Z||000002||turbo86se||05-26-2000||07:41 PM||||Thanks batboy,<BR>when I put the wheel back on, I made sure to evenly tighten the lug nuts, maybe that's where I went wrong. I also pulled back the dust shield a little more. <BR>Just got back from a test drive, NO NOISE!!  Went down this long stretch of road, everything is good. Got a little too excited and got into the turbo a little bit. Damn that thing's fast!!!!!<P>Leaving in three weeks today for the Fiero show in VA!!!!! Can't wait!!!||||reg||1
